<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">May Coup (Serbia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1903</span> · Also known as May Overthrow</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The May Coup was the assassination of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-obrenovic">Alexander Obrenović</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and his wife Draga by army officers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> in June 1903 (May by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-calendar">Julian calendar</a>). The conspirators, many later linked to the Black Hand, brought Peter I Karađorđević to the throne, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obrenovic-dynasty">Obrenović dynasty</a> and turning Serbia away from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/may-coup-serbia.jpg" alt="May Coup (Serbia)" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Le Petit Parisien · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Le_Petit_Parisien_-_May_Overthrow.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
